{"t":1794947118025,"type":"FeatureCollection","features":[{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1b79e2369a65d3d53cd09b2d82bcdcea2177543a.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-98.8,28.17],[-98.59,28.36],[-98.33,28.45],[-98.33,28.33],[-98.54,28.26],[-98.8,28.07],[-98.8,28.17]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1b79e2369a65d3d53cd09b2d82bcdcea2177543a.001.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1b79e2369a65d3d53cd09b2d82bcdcea2177543a.001.1","areaDesc":"McMullen, TX","geocode":{"SAME":["048311"],"UGC":["TXC311"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/TXC311"],"references":[{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e6fed5e1a746b19128188e41dda3f2b1cf46a5d6.001.1","identifier":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e6fed5e1a746b19128188e41dda3f2b1cf46a5d6.001.1","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-11-16T19:31:00-06:00"}],"sent":"2026-11-17T08:27:00-06:00","effective":"2026-11-17T08:27:00-06:00","onset":"2026-11-17T08:27:00-06:00","expires":"2026-11-17T23:30:00-06:00","ends":"2026-11-18T19:36:00-06:00","status":"Actual","messageType":"Update","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Observed","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Flood Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Corpus Christi TX","headline":"Flood Warning issued November 17 at 8:27AM CST until November 18 at 7:36PM CST by NWS Corpus Christi TX","description":"...The Flood Warning continues for the following rivers in Texas...\n\nNueces River Near Tilden affecting McMullen County.\n\nFor the Nueces River...including Cotulla, Tilden, Three Rivers,\nMathis, Bluntzer, Calallen...Minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is occurring and minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...Nueces River near Tilden.\n\n* WHEN...Until Wednesday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 15.0 feet, Much of the flood plain below cotulla to\nbelow tilden is cut off, as sloughs and peripheral channels fill.\nHunting cabins, oil field pump jacks and tank batteries flood well\naway from the channel. Livestock are cut off and can drown.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 7:30 AM CST Tuesday the stage was 15.3 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 11.0 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to fall below flood stage late\ntonight and continue falling to 11.0 feet by Sunday morning.\n- Flood stage is 14.0 feet.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nPlease report observed flooding to local emergency services or law\nenforcement and request they pass this information to the National\nWeather Service when you can do so safely.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov/crp.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSCRP"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS84 KCRP 171427"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING NOW IN EFFECT UNTIL WEDNESDAY EVENING"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.EXT.KCRP.FL.W.0029.000000T0000Z-261119T0136Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-11-18T19:36:00-06:00"],"expiredReferences":["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.3c8cb3a85de63662615e82aa3de94fc649624fe8.001.1,2026-11-16T09:44:00-06:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e98fa667dbddb33c715d8cc82aefe3f3184d0bd2.001.1,2026-11-15T19:36:00-06:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.884a2986aa03c1fa0b7e8fbbfb4797ef2b10d698.001.1,2026-11-15T13:30:00-06:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.40b6170256c15c4006bf8dd75dcb4052240655a5.001.1,2026-11-15T09:47:00-06:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.bdf26212e0aefd846b02a927ce0356e50037a4d5.001.1,2026-11-14T19:02:00-06:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.345324fc558f5c9e6675fb3c22721808d96fc4a3.001.1,2026-11-14T08:54:00-06:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.3cfa0b70a6989855fa7c22e761815c65c7a1afe4.001.1,2026-11-13T20:06:00-06:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.fbd7c04b6ed4e0eb360466d1a792c42b6fc9faf9.001.1,2026-11-13T08:17:00-06:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.79f54306900ef4f7373e0c7a36f1cc25dcf1b383.001.1,2026-11-12T18:55:00-06:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.18e883687f46e7c2a345a1cd781a4152492db08b.001.1,2026-11-12T08:31:00-06:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["FLS"],"NationalWeatherService":["FLW"]}}},{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.294e0e35d092b271b6bdce4212b3259093070008.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-111.78,34.83],[-111.79,34.81],[-111.82,34.8],[-111.84,34.8],[-111.84,34.82],[-111.81,34.83],[-111.78,34.85],[-111.77,34.87],[-111.76,34.9],[-111.72,34.94],[-111.63,34.95],[-111.61,34.94],[-111.61,34.9],[-111.63,34.87],[-111.65,34.87],[-111.68,34.89],[-111.7,34.91],[-111.72,34.91],[-111.73,34.89],[-111.75,34.86],[-111.78,34.83]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.294e0e35d092b271b6bdce4212b3259093070008.001.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.294e0e35d092b271b6bdce4212b3259093070008.001.1","areaDesc":"Coconino, AZ; Yavapai, AZ","geocode":{"SAME":["004005","004025"],"UGC":["AZC005","AZC025"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/AZC005","https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/AZC025"],"references":[],"sent":"2026-11-17T13:00:00-07:00","effective":"2026-11-17T13:00:00-07:00","onset":"2026-11-17T13:00:00-07:00","expires":"2026-11-17T18:00:00-07:00","ends":"2026-11-17T18:00:00-07:00","status":"Actual","messageType":"Alert","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Likely","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Flash Flood Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Flagstaff AZ","headline":"Flash Flood Warning issued November 17 at 1:00PM MST until November 17 at 6:00PM MST by NWS Flagstaff AZ","description":"FFWFGZ\n\nThe National Weather Service in Flagstaff has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nCoconino County in north central Arizona...\nYavapai County in west central Arizona...\n\n* Until 600 PM MST.\n\n* At 100 PM MST, River gages in Munds Canyon indicated over 3 feet of\nrises and levels were still rising. This water will the work\nthrough the Munds Park area and into Oak Creek this afternoon.\nFlash flooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Radar and river gage indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams,\nnormally dry washes, urban areas, highways, streets and\nunderpasses.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nSedona, Munds Park, Indian Gardens, Uptown Sedona, Red Rock State\nPark and Cathedral Rock.\n\nThis includes the following highways...\nInterstate 17 between mile markers 318 and 323. State Route 179\nbetween mile markers 311 and 313. State Route 89A between mile\nmarkers 374 and 379.\n\nThis includes the following swimming holes...\nMidgely Bridge, Buddha Beach \"Red Rock Crossing\" and Crescent Moon\nRanch.\n\nThis includes the following creeks, washes and rivers...\nOak Creek, Turkey Creek and Dry Beaver Creek.","instruction":"Flooding of washes and creeks will occur, some dirt roads will become\nmuddy and impassable. Paved roads and underpasses could become\nflooded as well.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FFWFGZ"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS55 KFGZ 172000"],"flashFloodDetection":["RADAR INDICATED"],"flashFloodDamageThreat":["CONSIDERABLE"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.NEW.KFGZ.FF.W.0219.261117T2000Z-261118T0100Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-11-17T18:00:00-07:00"],"WEAHandling":["Imminent Threat"],"CMAMtext":["NWS: FLASH FLOOD WARNING this area til 6:00 PM MST. Avoid flooded areas."],"CMAMlongtext":["National Weather Service: A FLASH FLOOD WARNING is in effect for this area until 6:00 PM MST. This is a dangerous and life-threatening situation. Do not attempt to travel unless you are fleeing an area subject to flooding or under an evacuation order."]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["FFW"],"NationalWeatherService":["FFW"]}}},{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.2ab0dcba67e466e668b37501d5d7ce7c9754bce6.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-80.99,28.54],[-80.9,28.55],[-80.8,28.35],[-80.72,28.05],[-80.99,28.54]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.2ab0dcba67e466e668b37501d5d7ce7c9754bce6.001.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.2ab0dcba67e466e668b37501d5d7ce7c9754bce6.001.1","areaDesc":"Brevard, FL","geocode":{"SAME":["012009"],"UGC":["FLC009"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/FLC009"],"references":[{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.4d24dcf3b1dca46b1c14a715c8538e8db6169665.001.1","identifier":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.4d24dcf3b1dca46b1c14a715c8538e8db6169665.001.1","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-11-16T20:20:00-05:00"}],"sent":"2026-11-17T09:21:00-05:00","effective":"2026-11-17T09:21:00-05:00","onset":"2026-11-17T09:21:00-05:00","expires":"2026-11-17T23:00:00-05:00","ends":null,"status":"Actual","messageType":"Update","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Observed","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Flood Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Melbourne FL","headline":"Flood Warning issued November 17 at 9:21AM EST by NWS Melbourne FL","description":"...The Flood Warning continues for the following rivers in Florida...\n\nSt Johns River Near Cocoa 9w affecting Brevard County.\n\n.Recent extreme rainfall over the headwaters of the St. Johns River\nhas caused the river near Cocoa to rise to Major Flood Stage. The\nriver is forecast to continue to remain steady with slight deviations\nin river levels through mid to late week due to additional forecast\nheavy rainfall.\n\nFor the St. Johns River...including Cocoa 9w...Major flooding is\nforecast.\n\n* WHAT...Major flooding is occurring and major flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...St Johns River near Cocoa 9w.\n\n* WHEN...Until further notice.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 17.2 feet, Water enters homes along the St Johns River\nin the Lake Poinsett area west of Cocoa, also low lying homes in\nthe Silver Pines subdivision in Rockledge and the Shakespeare Park\narea of Cocoa. Providence Road area west of Cocoa becomes\nimpassable, cutting off access to homes in the Mullet Lane and Bass\nRoad area. Docks flooded and water in parking lot at Lone Cabbage\nFish Camp.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 8:15 AM EST Tuesday the stage was 17.1 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 15.8 feet.\n- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending\nat 8:15 AM EST Tuesday was 17.1 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to remain steady above flood\nstage at 17.1 to 17.2 feet.\n- Flood stage is 16.0 feet.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Motorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov.\n\nThe next statement will be issued this evening at 1100 PM EST.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSMLB"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS82 KMLB 171421"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL FURTHER NOTICE"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.CON.KMLB.FL.W.0006.000000T0000Z-000000T0000Z/"],"expiredReferences":["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1ca005f84bb2b4a825c2afb3274f005a72bbfc98.002.1,2026-11-16T09:49:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.go