0135c2961a10b4ac7402fc57707e12c7c8.001.1","areaDesc":"Straits of Florida from Halfmoon Shoal to 20 NM west of Dry Tortugas out 20 NM; Straits of Florida from Halfmoon Shoal to 20 NM west of Dry Tortugas 20 to 60 NM out","geocode":{"SAME":["077055","077075"],"UGC":["GMZ055","GMZ075"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/forecast/GMZ055","https://api.weather.gov/zones/forecast/GMZ075"],"references":[],"sent":"2026-11-17T15:16:00-05:00","effective":"2026-11-17T15:16:00-05:00","onset":"2026-11-17T15:16:00-05:00","expires":"2026-11-17T16:15:00-05:00","ends":"2026-11-17T16:15:00-05:00","status":"Actual","messageType":"Alert","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Likely","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Special Marine Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Key West FL","headline":"Special Marine Warning issued November 17 at 3:16PM EST until November 17 at 4:15PM EST by NWS Key West FL","description":"SMWKEY\n\nThe National Weather Service in Key West has issued a\n\n* Special Marine Warning for...\nStraits of Florida from Halfmoon Shoal to 20 nm west of Dry\nTortugas out 60 nm...\n\n* Until 415 PM EST.\n\n* At 316 PM EST, a possible strong waterspout was located 11 nm south\nof Tortugas Ecological Reserve South, moving east at 10 knots.\n\nHAZARD...Waterspouts, wind gusts 34 knots or greater, and large\nhail.\n\nSOURCE...National Weather Service Meteorologist.\n\nIMPACT...Waterspouts can quickly form and capsize boats, cause\nconsiderable damage to vessels and create suddenly higher\nwaves. Expect wind gusts in excess of 34 knots, suddenly\nhigher waves, frequent lightning, and heavy downpours.\nLarge hail could result in injury and damage to boats.\n\n* The possible strong waterspout will remain over mainly open waters.","instruction":"Prepare for wind gusts in excess of 34 knots, steep and fast-building\nseas, frequent lightning, and blinding downpours. Stay low or go\nbelow, and make sure all on board are wearing life jackets.\n\nWaterspouts can easily overturn boats and create locally hazardous\nseas. Seek safe harbor immediately.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["SMWKEY"],"WMOidentifier":["WHUS52 KKEY 172016"],"eventMotionDescription":["2026-11-17T20:16:00-00:00...storm...287DEG...9KT...24.25,-83.1"],"waterspoutDetection":["POSSIBLE"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.NEW.KKEY.MA.W.0367.261117T2016Z-261117T2115Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-11-17T16:15:00-05:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["SMW"],"NationalWeatherService":["MAW"]}}},{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cd2a32c09604bbb4ce3dbd25f55fa89188207a8c.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-113.33,32.97],[-113.24,33.01],[-113.19,33.03],[-113.17,33.04],[-113.14,33.06],[-113.1,33.08],[-113.07,33.1],[-113.05,33.11],[-113.01,33.11],[-113,33.08],[-113.02,33.07],[-113.03,33.06],[-113.04,33.04],[-113.11,33],[-113.19,32.97],[-113.49,32.84],[-113.56,32.83],[-113.58,32.88],[-113.47,32.91],[-113.37,32.95],[-113.33,32.97]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cd2a32c09604bbb4ce3dbd25f55fa89188207a8c.001.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cd2a32c09604bbb4ce3dbd25f55fa89188207a8c.001.1","areaDesc":"Maricopa, AZ; Yuma, AZ","geocode":{"SAME":["004013","004027"],"UGC":["AZC013","AZC027"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/AZC013","https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/AZC027"],"references":[{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cbd7a3fa364ff386d3a742b5a39a8f8c52a72ebf.001.1","identifier":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cbd7a3fa364ff386d3a742b5a39a8f8c52a72ebf.001.1","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-11-12T11:41:00-07:00"},{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.bc383b500d053c6b9ea8166be008d9fcb26ed469.001.1","identifier":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.bc383b500d053c6b9ea8166be008d9fcb26ed469.001.1","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-11-13T19:24:00-07:00"},{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6919edc7e119bce46062e3c64c5e3fd608b5c01f.001.1","identifier":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6919edc7e119bce46062e3c64c5e3fd608b5c01f.001.1","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-11-10T08:00:00-07:00"},{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c6ce1e79c6e03fc4627ccbfc4f48df38490db583.001.1","identifier":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c6ce1e79c6e03fc4627ccbfc4f48df38490db583.001.1","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-11-11T11:41:00-07:00"}],"sent":"2026-11-17T08:21:00-07:00","effective":"2026-11-17T08:21:00-07:00","onset":"2026-11-17T08:21:00-07:00","expires":"2026-11-24T11:00:00-07:00","ends":"2026-11-24T11:00:00-07:00","status":"Actual","messageType":"Update","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Likely","urgency":"Expected","event":"Flood Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Phoenix AZ","headline":"Flood Warning issued November 17 at 8:21AM MST until November 24 at 11:00AM MST by NWS Phoenix AZ","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by upstream dam release continues.\n\n* WHERE...Maricopa County in south central Arizona...\nNortheastern Yuma County in southwestern Arizona...\n\n* WHEN...Until 1100 AM MST Tuesday Nov 24.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is expected. Low-water crossings are\nlikely to become inundated with water and may not be passable.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 815 AM MST, water releases from Painted Rock Dam continue with\nflow peaking around 3000 cfs. A streamflow gauge immediately\ndownstream also indicated a stage near 10 feet.\n- Flooding is expected along the Gila River.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nFarmlands and low-water crossings along the Gila River.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLWPSR"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS45 KPSR 171521"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING FOR THE UPSTREAM RELEASE OF PAINTED ROCK DAM ON THE GILA RIVER NOW IN EFFECT UNTIL 11 AM MST TUESDAY"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.EXT.KPSR.FA.W.0044.000000T0000Z-261124T1800Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-11-24T11:00:00-07:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["FLW"],"NationalWeatherService":["FAW"]}}},{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e2e31c24b8041ae6d756ab51ac1361073e194021.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-81.23,28.7],[-81.17,28.79],[-81,28.73],[-80.9,28.54],[-81.23,28.7]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e2e31c24b8041ae6d756ab51ac1361073e194021.001.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e2e31c24b8041ae6d756ab51ac1361073e194021.001.1","areaDesc":"Seminole, FL","geocode":{"SAME":["012117"],"UGC":["FLC117"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/FLC117"],"references":[{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d70614b02234695c99b688b435cd627247480aa3.001.1","identifier":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d70614b02234695c99b688b435cd627247480aa3.001.1","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-11-16T20:22:00-05:00"}],"sent":"2026-11-17T09:23:00-05:00","effective":"2026-11-17T09:23:00-05:00","onset":"2026-11-17T09:23:00-05:00","expires":"2026-11-17T23:00:00-05:00","ends":null,"status":"Actual","messageType":"Update","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Observed","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Flood Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Melbourne FL","headline":"Flood Warning issued November 17 at 9:23AM EST by NWS Melbourne FL","description":"...The Flood Warning continues for the following rivers in Florida...\n\nSt Johns River Near Above Lake Harney affecting Seminole County.\n\n.Heavy rainfall over recent weeks has caused river levels on the St.\nJohns near Geneva Above Lake Harney to reach Moderate Flood Stage.\nRiver levels are expected slowly rise into this weekend through\nModerate Flood Stage due to additional heavy rainfall over the basin.\n\nFor the St. Johns River...including Above Lake Harney...Major\nflooding is forecast.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is occurring and moderate flooding is\nforecast.\n\n* WHERE...St Johns River near Above Lake Harney.\n\n* WHEN...Until further notice.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 9.3 feet, Many secondary roads are flooded near Lake\nHarney. Flooding in the Hatbill Road area near Loughman Lake.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 8:30 AM EST Tuesday the stage was 9.0 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 6.0 feet.\n- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending\nat 8:30 AM EST Tuesday was 9.0 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to remain steady above flood\nstage at 9.0 to 9.2 feet.\n- Flood stage is 8.0 feet.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Motorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov.\n\nThe next statement will be issued this evening at 1100 PM EST.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSMLB"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS82 KMLB 171423"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL FURTHER NOTICE"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.CON.KMLB.FL.W.0007.000000T0000Z-000000T0000Z/"],"expiredReferences":["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1ca005f84bb2b4a825c2afb3274f005a72bbfc98.001.1,2026-11-1